I assume the mechanics is the same as in vanilla. All covetous
monsters don't just walk about the dungeon. No, they simple appear
wherever the wish -- and this action is not the same as teleportation
(it is sometimes called "warping") and therefore it is not subject to
non-teleport level limitation (aka "mysterious force").

Anyway, why you didn't just use Elbereth? When facing Demogorgon, the
first thing to do is to burn permanent Elbereth and then heal. The
Demo will not attack you while you are on E, so even if you try and
fail to teleport, you'll still remain safe. Another thing is that
fighting Demogorgon burdened is an elementary mistake.

